'' =============================================================================
'' Single-Step Debugger Test Program 10 — Smart pin watch
''
'' Covers Test Plan test:
''   Test 10 — Smart pin delta tracking, DIR-only filter, RQPIN readback
''
'' PASM-only program: cog 0 boots directly into this DAT at $000, so DEBUG_MAIN
'' breaks on the FIRST instruction (entry / dirl ...) — no Spin interpreter or
'' coginit indirection in the way.
''
'' Behavior: Configures pin 0 as an NCO-frequency smart pin at ~1 MHz, following
'' the documented init order (DIRL reset, WRPIN, WXPIN, enable via DIRH, THEN WYPIN
'' — see P2 KB %00110 NCO Frequency). With a real frequency and base period X=1, the
'' Z phase accumulator advances every clock and overflows continuously, so the pin's
'' IN flag is raised on every debug poll — the debugger therefore reports pin 0, and
'' RQPIN (which reads Z) shows a rapidly changing 8-hex value in the SMART watch panel.
''
'' Y = round(2^32 * Fout * X / Fclk) for Fout = 1 MHz, X = 1, Fclk = 200 MHz
''   = 2^32 / 200 = $0147_AE14
''
'' WHY the earlier version showed nothing: it used `wypin #$FF` with `wxpin ##1000`,
'' so Z gained only 255 every 1000 clocks — a Z-overflow (and IN pulse) only about
'' once every 84 seconds. The debugger reports a smart pin when its result is ready
'' (IN raised), so pin 0 was essentially never reported → the watch stayed empty. It
'' also set WYPIN before DIRH (wrong init order), which the DIRH reset can clobber.
'' =============================================================================
CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_MAIN = 1

DAT
                org
entry           dirl    #0                       ' reset smart pin
                wrpin   ##P_NCO_FREQ, #0          ' NCO frequency mode
                wxpin   #1, #0                    ' base period X = 1 clock (max resolution)
                dirh    #0                       ' enable FIRST (documented init order)
                wypin   ##$0147_AE14, #0          ' THEN set frequency (~1 MHz)
.loop           rqpin   pa, #0                    ' read NCO phase accumulator (Z)
                jmp     #.loop
